Z||000013||Formula88||11-13-2001||02:27 PM||||Be careful with a disconnected EGR.  If you're not using a chip to retune the car for the missing EGR, you can burn a piston.  I know lots of people have done it.  I've done it for a while myself.  Just making sure you're aware of the potential dangers.  I'd recommend running Premium fuel without the EGR connected.  Keep an eye on your spark plugs to make sure it doesn't look like your cylinders are burning too hot.||||reg||4
Z||000014||FieroFuker||11-13-2001||02:37 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Be careful with a disconnected EGR.  ....Keep an eye on your spark plugs to make sure it doesn't look like your cylinders are burning too hot.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>huh? burn a cyclinder? I known people who run daily cars all the time without egr... thats a bunch of hoo haa.. oh I run stock plugs.. those plat 4s dont run good with 2.8s and 2.5s try to eliminate all unneccsary vacuam tubes. (becarefull YOu need some of em   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>oh Remove your AC unit off the belt assembly<p>[This message has been edited by FieroFuker (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroFuker||11-13-2001||03:25 PM||||oh and I dont know if this improves power.. but take out the pcv valve and the tube to the intake on the valve covers and put in a couple  3/4 breathers (I think this keeps the engine from sucking used air from engine ... <BR>corect me if I'm wrong but I did this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
